On Tuesday, May 20, 2014 20:14:54 Gleki Arxokuna wrote:
> "by standard" place here is unlike other "by standard" places and serves to
> separate British mile from nautical mile. Am I wrong?

All the measurement words have a "by standard" place. The standard for the 
meter has been two marks on a metal bar, a count of wavelengths of light 
emitted by krypton, and a second with the speed of light fixed (the current 
standard).

I vote yes.

Another place inconsistency: "mitre" has a place for direction, whereas no 
other length unit does.

